course: dictionary
lesson: 4651
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The sentence tells you which meaning is right. «The show went on without a hitch.» A hitch is a small problem, but «without a hitch» means nothing went wrong, so the show ran smoothly.
explain: Look at the other words to find the meaning. «Hitch the horse to the cart» uses hitch as a verb, meaning fasten one thing to another. The word «to» and the cart are clues: you are joining two things together.
explain: «He hitched up his trousers» means he pulled them up quickly. Words like «up» and the action help you decide. Always check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
fact: «Hitch» can be a noun or a verb. As a noun, a hitch is a small problem that delays something, as in «a technical hitch».
fact: «Hitch» as a verb means to fasten something to something else, as in «hitch a trailer to the car».
fact: «Get hitched» is informal and means get married.
fact: A clove hitch is a knot used to tie a rope to a post or ring. Scouts and guides learn knots like this.
fact: Never hitch rides with strangers. Only ever travel with a trusted adult.
exercise: «The school play went on without a hitch.» What does without a hitch mean? | *Everything went smoothly, with no problems | The play was cancelled | Everyone arrived late | Something was lost and nobody knew where it was
exercise: «Dad will hitch the trailer to the car.» What does hitch mean here? | *To fasten one thing to another | To pull something up quickly | To get married | A small problem
exercise: «He hitched up his trousers and ran.» What does hitched up mean? | *Pulled them up quickly | Took them off | Bought a new pair | Tied them into a knot on the floor
test: Scouts learn the clove hitch. What is a clove hitch? | A type of song sung at camp | A kind of bird that lives near water | A cake baked in a round tin | *A knot used to tie a rope to a post or ring
test: Tom is walking home when a stranger in a car offers him a lift. What should he do? | Get in quickly, because it is raining | Ask the stranger for money first | *Say no and tell a trusted adult | Hitch a ride with the stranger
exam: «A tiny tick can hitch a ride on your leg without you feeling it.» What does hitch a ride mean here? | To stop walking and sit down | *To travel by clinging on to something, as a free passenger | To pay for a taxi with coins | To break a leg
